{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "02", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "20", "M": "13", "S": "21"}}, "news": [{"title": "Merlin Group plans \u20b910,000 crore investment over five years; targets \u20b9700 crore sales in FY27", "para": "Merlin Group plans to deploy about \u20b910,000 crore over the next five years across residential, commercial, retail and mixed-use projects, said Sushil Mohta, chairman, Merlin Group and president, CREDAI West Bengal. The developer, which recorded sales of around \u20b9500 crore in FY26, is targeting about \u20b9700 crore in FY27 and has nearly 20 million sq ft of development potential lined up for launch over the next two-three years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/merlin-group-plans-10000-crore-investment-over-five-years-targets-700-crore-sales-in-fy27/134644953?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-93344/134644953.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Old legislations impeding development must go: West Bengal finance minister", "para": "West Bengal finance minister Swapan Dasgupta said legacy land laws, including the Urban Land (Ceiling and Regulation) Act, need to be reviewed or removed where they restrict development, as the state seeks to attract organised developers and industrial investment. He also called for greater regulation, accountability and transparency in the real estate sector.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/old-legislations-impeding-development-must-go-west-bengal-finance-minister/134644796?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-45616/134644796.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Ajmera Realty looks to create two million sq ft of rental portfolio  in Mumbai over next 5-8 years", "para": "Ajmera Realty & Infra (India) is targeting \u20b92,200 crore of pre-sales in FY27 and expects to invest over \u20b91,000 crore across its existing and upcoming projects over the next three-four years, said Dhaval Ajmera, director-corporate affairs. The company is also looking to build around two million sq ft of rental assets in Mumbai over the next five-eight years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/ajmera-realty-looks-to-create-two-million-sq-ft-of-rental-portfolio-in-mumbai-over-next-5-8-years/134644415?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-88070/134644415.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}